### Core Aggregation Patterns in Java

When building backend services and solving algorithmic problems, Map data structures form the backbone of two primary data transformations:

---

### Pattern 1: Frequency Counters & Histograms

A frequency counter measures the occurrence count of distinct tokens in $O(N)$ time:
```java
Map<String, Integer> counts = new HashMap<>();
for (String token : tokens) {
    counts.merge(token, 1, Integer::sum);
}
```
This enables instantaneous $O(1)$ lookups for item frequency, finding majority elements, or identifying the first non-repeating character in a stream.

---

### Pattern 2: Multimap Grouping ($K \to \text{List}\langle V\rangle$)

Java does not provide a native `MultiMap` in `java.util`, but you can cleanly model it using:
```java
Map<K, List<V>> multiMap = new HashMap<>();
multiMap.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(value);
```
`computeIfAbsent` ensures that list initialization is atomic, lazy, and free of noisy `contains` checks.

---

### Pattern 3: Canonical Anagram Grouping in Code

```java
import java.util.*;

public class MapGroupingDemo {
    public static List<List<String>> groupAnagrams(String[] words) {
        if (words == null || words.length == 0) return List.of();

        Map<String, List<String>> anagramMap = new HashMap<>();
        for (String word : words) {
            // Compute canonical key: sorted characters
            char[] chars = word.toCharArray();
            Arrays.sort(chars);
            String canonicalKey = new String(chars);

            anagramMap.computeIfAbsent(canonicalKey, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(word);
        }
        return new ArrayList<>(anagramMap.values());
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[] sample = {"eat", "tea", "tan", "ate", "nat", "bat"};
        List<List<String>> grouped = groupAnagrams(sample);
        System.out.println("Grouped Anagrams: " + grouped);
    }
}
```

**Console Output:**
```text
Grouped Anagrams: [[eat, tea, ate], [bat], [tan, nat]]
```

---

### Complexity Analysis of Grouping Patterns

| Operation | Time Complexity | Auxiliary Space |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Token Frequency Tally** | $O(N)$ | $O(U)$ where $U$ = unique tokens |
| **Anagram Grouping** | $O(N \cdot K \log K)$ ($K$ = word length) | $O(N \cdot K)$ |
| **Multimap Inversion** | $O(N)$ | $O(N)$ |

